      "sign": "B. Volkmann (Stuttgart)"
     },
     "text": "The following theorem is proved: For any set \\(A\\subseteq \\mathbb R^k\\) with upper metric density \\(\\delta (A)>0\\) and any set \\(V=\\{x_1,\\dots,x_k\\}\\subseteq \\mathbb R^k\\) spanning a nondegenerate \\((k-1)\\)-dimensional simplex, there exists a number \\(\\lambda_0\\) such that \\(A\\) contains an isometric image of \\(\\lambda V\\) for any \\(\\lambda >\\lambda_0\\). The case \\(k=2\\) had been proved by Y. Katznelson and B. Weiss (preprint) [see also H. Furstenberg, Y. Katznelson and B. Weiss, Mathematics of Ramsey theory, Coll. Pap. Symp. Graph Theory, Prague/Czech., Algorithms Comb. 5, 184--198 (1990; Zbl 0738.28013)]. \n\n\nIn an appendix the author establishes a result on double integrals over compact abelian groups from which \\textit{K. F. Roth}'s celebrated pre-Szemer\u00e9di theorem on arithmetic progressions follows [J. Lond. Math. Soc. 28, 104--109 (1953; Zbl 0050.04002)].",
     "contribution_type": "review"
    }
   ],
